# Tier B: the preview pane — an image, code with syntax colouring, two megabytes of text, and the
# same two megabytes as hex.
#
# A selection loads the preview off-thread; each sample chains the selection with `settle-preview`,
# which waits for that load to start and finish, so the number is "clicked to shown" rather than
# "clicked". Only a selection that follows another within 150 ms waits for the sweep to end first, so
# a `settle 200` before each sample makes it a click after a pause, which loads at once.

preview-fixture
write Preview/Big.txt 2000000
write-binary Preview/Big.bin 2000000
go Preview
preview on
settle 200
time preview.png select sample.png; settle-preview
assert-preview image
settle 200
time preview.code select Sample.cs; settle-preview
assert-preview text
settle 200
time preview.text2mb select Big.txt; settle-preview
assert-preview text
settle 200
time preview.hex2mb select Big.bin; preview-mode hex; settle-preview
assert-preview hex
preview-mode auto
mem preview
assert-not-launched
